PRE-REGISTRATION -- full-catalogue choosability run            2026-09-12
Written BEFORE the run. The 30-skill result is known; this fixes what the
145-skill result will be allowed to mean, so neither outcome can be read
into the recommendation after the fact.

WHAT THE 30-SKILL RUN SETTLED AND DID NOT
  settled: NAMES is decisively worse. 9-0 discordant vs FULL (exact two-sided
           sign test p=0.0039), 8-1 vs FIRST (p=0.0391). The ADR's "probably
           too cryptic" guess is CONFIRMED; the 97% saving is not available.
  NOT settled: FIRST vs FULL. Only 4 discordant pairs, split 3-1, p=0.6250.
           Underpowered, not equal. The recommendation is neither vindicated
           nor retracted by that run.
  noise floor: ZERO. Two separate process invocations returned byte-identical
           scores (15/13/6) and identical misses. So repetition buys nothing;
           only a larger population can separate FIRST from FULL.

POPULATION
  All 145 skills that yield a usable body-derived query. No sampling, so the
  30-skill draw's unlucky composition (aspirations-* 7 of 30 against 3.1
  expected; 14 of 30 in a >=3-member sibling family) cannot apply. Queries and
  rendering are UNCHANGED from the 30-skill run -- only the population grows.

PRIMARY -- FULL vs FIRST, paired exact two-sided sign test on discordant pairs
  p <  0.05 and FULL ahead -> the second addendum's recommendation is RETRACTED.
        Name+first-sentence measurably loses choosability; the 66% saving costs
        accuracy and must not be built on the strength of this ADR.
  p <  0.05 and FIRST ahead -> a surprise; record it, do not act on it this pass.
  p >= 0.05 -> the two shapes are indistinguishable ACROSS THE WHOLE CATALOGUE.
        The recommendation is SAFE TO BUILD. Report the bound: with n discordant
        pairs, state the largest true difference this run could still have missed
        rather than claiming equality.

SECONDARY -- FULL vs NAMES
  Expected to reconfirm the 30-skill finding. If it does NOT reproduce at n=145,
  the 30-skill result was a sampling artifact and the "too cryptic" confirmation
  is withdrawn along with it.

CONTROL -- FULL is the positive control, as before
  VOID the run if FULL scores below 25%. Deliberately NOT set at the observed
  50%: a boundary placed at the value it is tested against is satisfiable by
  stasis and carries almost no information (guard-5645). 25% is far above the
  0.7% chance rate of a 145-way choice, so it still catches a dead instrument.
  An empty completion aborts the run as an INSTRUMENT failure, never scores as
  a wrong answer (guard-6562).

WHAT WILL NOT BE DONE
  No re-scoring to a laxer "right family" metric. Exact match was registered and
  stays. The sibling-confusion structure is a NEW question for a future run, not
  a re-reading of this one.
